    1. Pick grid size in range 13-14 x 12-15.
    2. Decide object count (6-7). For each, pick random rectangle dims h in [2,4], w in [2,6].
    3. Assign each object a marker count -- 3 objects get 0 or 1 (kept), rest get 2-4 (removed).
    4. Place rectangles on grid with Chebyshev gap >= 2 between all pairs. Use greedy random placement with rejection.
    5. Fill each rectangle with dense color, then randomly replace marker_count cells with marker color.
    6. Verify total marker pixels in 9-14 and dense/marker ratio reasonable; retry assignment if not.
```
