<description>
Complete each marked object by mirroring its trusted side across the yellow axis.

Input structure:
- The background is black.
- Each transformed object has one non-yellow foreground color plus yellow
  pixels.
- Its yellow pixels contain one contiguous horizontal or vertical mirror
  axis and at least one off-axis yellow control pixel.

Rule:
- For every object with a yellow axis, use the side containing the off-axis
  yellow control pixel as the source side.
- Reflect the whole rectangular source half of the object's bounding box
  across the axis, copying both foreground and background pixels onto the
  opposite side.
- Leave the source side, the axis, and unrelated pixels unchanged unless
  they fall inside a reflected target half.

Key insight:
- The extra yellow pixel is not another object detail; it marks which half
  of the pattern is correct and should overwrite the other half by symmetry.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "symmetry/pattern",
  "src": "each foreground object containing a contiguous yellow horizontal or vertical axis and an off-axis yellow control pixel",
  "dst": "opposite half of the same object region across the yellow axis",
  "transform": "use the side containing the off-axis yellow control pixel as the source; reflect that rectangular half across the axis, copying background too so conflicting pixels on the other side are erased"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 14-28 rows x 14-28 cols, black background
  objects:
    count: 1-4 yellow-axis objects per grid, each with a unique non-yellow foreground color
    bbox: 3-9 rows x 6-10 cols per object
    content: irregular blob of one foreground color, ~63-81% fill in source half
    axis: contiguous yellow line (H or V), spanning 57-100% of bbox cross-dimension
    control_pixel: exactly 1 off-axis yellow pixel, perpendicular distance = 2 from axis, within axis span
    halves: source half >= target half (equal or source 1 row/col larger)
    damage: target half is a garbled version of source (~28-50% of pixels differ from correct mirror)
    damage may include stray same-color pixels disconnected from main body [observed]
  layout: object bboxes (including reflected extension) non-overlapping, >=2 cells gap [observed]
  transform:
    reflect source half across yellow axis, overwriting target half
    control pixel also gets reflected, creating a symmetric yellow marker on the other side

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Choose grid size and number of objects (1-4)
    2. For each object, build the OUTPUT (symmetric) version first
       a. Pick orientation (H or V), foreground color, bbox size (3-9 x 6-10)
       b. Pick axis position within bbox (source_half >= target_half, diff 0-1)
       c. Draw an irregular connected blob on the source half (~65-80% fill)
